{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>I hated</b> — If you say: all the days that we offer burnt offerings, no evil is seen; therefore he said: I hated." "<b>Your festivals</b> — like כבשיכם אסרו חג בעבותים חגים ינקופו [your rams bound the festival with ropes, festivals will cut off]." "<b>and I will not smell</b> — a smell on the day of your assembly. For if you offer burnt offerings that you are not obligated in, and meal offerings to appease me, I will not smell."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The quotation is from Hosea 9:5 (with some variation); Ibn Ezra cites it as a wordplay on the root חג. The phrase as quoted is textually difficult and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:12.259222112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}